				33,
				6
			],
			"Message": "chore(Air): Standardize path expansion and fix type safety\n\nThis commit refines the Air daemon's implementation to improve consistency and type safety across its background services (downloader, indexing, updates). The changes align with Land's architectural principle of centralized configuration management and robust error handling.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Centralized all path expansion logic to use `ConfigurationManager::expand_path` in Downloader, Indexing, and Updates modules, eliminating redundant helper functions and ensuring consistent path resolution\n- Fixed CPU usage calculation in ApplicationState by adding explicit `as f64` cast to prevent potential integer overflow and ensure accurate system metrics reporting\n- Added missing imports (`toml` dependency for configuration parsing, `SecureRandom` for authentication cryptography, `Platform` trait for systemstat integration) to resolve compilation issues and support future features\n- Corrected reference in Updates module to use `app_state.configuration.downloader.cache_directory` instead of local config variable, ensuring proper configuration hierarchy\n\nThese changes enhance the Air daemon's reliability and maintainability, supporting its role as a critical background service provider within the Land ecosystem.",
			"SHA": "9f9d4341522fef711ad191f9f5f9919277bed00d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-28T08:40:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				33,
				7
			],
			"Message": "chore(Air): Refine code quality and remove redundancies\n\nThis commit performs targeted code cleanups in the Air daemon, which provides essential background services (downloader, indexing, updates) for the Land ecosystem. The changes focus on improving maintainability and aligning with Rust best practices:\n\n- Simplified system metrics collection in `ApplicationState` by directly using `System::new()` instead of redundant error wrapping\n- Fixed error handling in `Authentication` service's encryption key generation to properly chain error mappings\n- Removed unused imports (`toml` in `Configuration`, `tokio_stream` in `Downloader` and `Updates`) to reduce clutter\n- Updated stream extensions from `tokio_stream` to `futures` for consistency with workspace dependency management\n- Eliminated unnecessary re-exports in `Library.rs` and redundant `#[tonic::async_trait]` attribute in the gRPC service implementation\n\nThese refinements ensure the Air daemon's codebase is cleaner and more efficient, supporting reliable operation within the Land architecture's service layer.",
			"SHA": "88544f1ac13d83eebc5bdf8fdee4e791683af9bb"
		},
